# Line endings.
#
# Without this file git stored whatever bytes a tool happened to write, so
# an editor or script that rewrote a CRLF file with LF endings produced a
# whole-file diff with the real change buried inside it. That happened
# twice on 2026-08-31: a fifteen line edit to WoW-Companion.pyw was
# recorded as roughly 2600 changed lines, and the actual change became
# unreviewable.
#
# text=auto stores text as LF in the repository whatever the working tree
# holds, so the same edit yields the same commit whichever tool wrote it.
#
# eol=lf pins the WORKING TREE to LF as well. Without it, text=auto with
# core.eol unset overrides this repo's deliberate local
# core.autocrlf=false on Git for Windows and starts writing CRLF into
# checkouts - a behaviour change nobody asked for.
#
# This IS accompanied by a one-time `git add --renormalize .`, and that is
# not optional. Since git 2.10 text=auto skips check-in normalisation for
# any path whose index blob already holds CRLF (the has_crlf_in_index
# guard in crlf_to_git), so a CRLF-preserving edit - what every Windows
# editor does by default - would commit those files still CRLF forever.
# Files already carrying CRLF would have stayed permanently outside the
# protection, which is exactly backwards: they are the ones most exposed
# to the bug. An earlier revision of this file claimed they would
# "normalise one at a time as they are next edited". They would not.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files, declared rather than left to heuristics. text=auto guesses
# from content, and a wrong guess on one of these corrupts it silently.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.zip binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary
*.bin binary
# WoW's own texture formats. Not tracked here today, but build_release.py
# copies addon Media folders wholesale, so name them before one arrives.
*.blp binary
*.tga binary
